  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(f(x) = ax + b\\) and \\(f^{-1}(x) = bx + a\\) with \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) real, what is the value of \\(a + b?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2004-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(f(f^{-1}(x)) = x,\\) we have \\(a(bx + a) + b = x.\\) Matching terms gives \\(ab = 1\\) and \\(a^2 + b = 0.\\) Then \\(b = \\frac{1}{a}\\) and \\(a^2 + \\frac{1}{a} = 0,\\) so \\(a^3 = -1,\\) giving \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = -1.\\) Thus \\(a + b = -2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(f(f^{-1}(x)) = x\\)",
        "Expanding \\(a(bx + a) + b = x\\) gives \\(ab = 1\\) and \\(a^2 + b = 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
